->Margin is a space between an element and other elements

====================================================
                   CSS MARGIN — CHEAT SHEET
====================================================

1) WHAT IS MARGIN?
----------------------------------------------------
• Margin is the empty space OUTSIDE an element's border.
• It creates space BETWEEN two elements.
• Margin pushes one element away from another.
• Think of it like "breathing room" around a box.


====================================================
       MARGIN vs PADDING (SUPER EASY DIFFERENCE)
====================================================
• Padding = INSIDE space (content → border)
• Margin  = OUTSIDE space (element → element)


====================================================
2) MARGIN SIDES (INDIVIDUAL PROPERTIES)
====================================================
margin-top:    10px;
margin-right:  20px;
margin-bottom: 15px;
margin-left:   5px;


====================================================
3) MARGIN SHORTHAND
====================================================
margin: 10px;
    → all four sides = 10px

margin: 10px 20px;
    → top-bottom = 10px
      left-right = 20px

margin: 10px 20px 5px;
    → top = 10px
      left-right = 20px
      bottom = 5px

margin: 10px 20px 5px 0;
    → top = 10px
      right = 20px
      bottom = 5px
      left = 0


====================================================
4) MARGIN COLLAPSE (IMPORTANT!!)
====================================================
• Only VERTICAL margins collapse (top + bottom).
• They do NOT add together… the larger one wins.

Example:
h1 { margin-bottom: 20px; }
h2 { margin-top: 30px; }

Actual space between them = 30px (NOT 50px)
The bigger margin dominates.

• Padding does NOT collapse — only margins do.

====================================================
1) NEGATIVE MARGINS
====================================================
margin-top: -20px;
→ Pulls the element upward.

• Padding cannot be negative
• Margin can be negative


====================================================
MEMORY TRICK (VERY USEFUL)
====================================================
Padding = inside the border  
Margin  = outside the border (between elements)
====================================================
